  "slug": "gland-development-mll4-4b67",
  "summary": "Six preprints apply statistical and sequence-based models to resolve cell types, composition and regulatory links from methylation, chromatin and multiome data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is attributing signal to specific cell types or states rather than to bulk averages or shared confounders. EPIC2 links GWAS summary statistics with single-cell chromatin accessibility to identify trait-relevant cell types. LongReadClock builds cell-type-resolved epigenetic clocks from bulk blood long-read methylation, separating composition effects. CREMAP adjusts latent shared technical and biological variation before testing peak-gene links in single-cell multiome data. EMBHER shows Borzoi sequence-to-function embeddings capture whole-blood expression heritability. A CHIP multi-omic study of 466 samples reports distinct effects across driver genes, and Pooch uses differentially methylated CpGs to assign parent of origin in Hi-C-phased assemblies. New here is the use of long-read methylation for cell-type-resolved ageing; all results are preprint-level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
